  "root_page": {
    "title": "Content Engine OS",
    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "text": "Welcome to Content Engine OS! This dashboard unifies your content pipeline, seasonal campaigns, sponsorships, and ideas into one cohesive publishing engine."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_1",
        "text": "Weekly Focus & Immediate Priorities"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Check off high-leverage production tasks before moving on to new brainstorm sessions."
      },
      {
        "type": "to_do",
        "text": "Finalize draft script for Notion 2024 walkthrough video"
      },
      {
        "type": "to_do",
        "text": "Review sponsored contract deliverables with Athletic Greens"
      },
      {
        "type": "to_do",
        "text": "Schedule Instagram Reels for next Monday through Wednesday"
      },
      {
        "type": "divider",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Publishing Master Workflow"
      },
      {
        "type": "numbered_list",
        "text": "1. Brainstorm & capture inspirations in the Content Ideas Backlog."
      },
      {
        "type": "numbered_list",
        "text": "2. Align validated ideas with a quarterly theme in Campaigns & Themes."
      },
      {
        "type": "numbered_list",
        "text": "3. Promote concepts into the Content Repository to schedule dates and track production stages."
      },
      {
        "type": "numbered_list",
        "text": "4. Link commercial deals via Brand Partners to keep sponsored deliverables accountable."
      },
      {
        "type": "quote",
        "text": "\"Consistency is not about perfection every day; it's about eliminating the friction between idea and execution.\""
      }
    ]
  },
  "sub_pages": [
    {
      "title": "How to Use This Template",
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "heading_1",
          "text": "System Architecture Overview"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Content Engine OS relies on four tightly coupled databases that eliminate duplicate data entry and streamline creator operations."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading_2",
          "text": "Database Breakdown"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Content Repository: The operational heartbeat. Holds all individual pieces across all channels with date tracking and production stages."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Campaigns & Themes: High-level strategic groups (e.g., quarterly themes, product launches) aggregating multiple posts."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Brand Partners: CRM for inbound and outbound sponsorships, track revenue per deliverable and client contacts."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Content Ideas Backlog: Zero-friction scratchpad for raw ideas and bookmarks before they enter active production."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading_2",
          "text": "Pro-Tips for Creators"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Keep your Ideas Backlog separate from your Calendar. Only drag ideas into the Content Repository when you have committed to a scheduled publishing date."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Repurposing & Distribution Playbook",
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "heading_1",
          "text": "The 1-to-5 Atomization Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Never publish a long-form piece of content without deriving at least 5 micro-assets from it. Maximize your output without extra filming time."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading_2",
          "text": "Standard Repurposing Matrix"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "YouTube Longform -> 3 Shorts / TikToks (highlighting specific tips or punchlines)."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Script Outline -> 1 In-depth LinkedIn slide carousel or Twitter/X thread."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Key Takeaways -> Weekend Newsletter edition linking back to the primary asset."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "When creating derivative posts, create separate rows in the Content Repository and connect them to the same Campaign for holistic attribution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sponsorship & Rate Card Guide",
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "heading_1",
          "text": "Monetization Guidelines"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Use these baseline rates and deliverable terms when quoting inbound brands or pitching sponsors."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading_2",
          "text": "Current Rate Card"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "YouTube Dedicated Video: $3,500 - $5,000 (Includes 1 integration + link in top 3 lines)."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "YouTube Mid-Roll Integration (60-90s): $1,800 - $2,500."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "Newsletter Primary Sponsor: $800 - $1,200 per issue."
        },
        {
          "type": "bulleted_list",
          "text": "LinkedIn Sponsored Post: $1,000 - $1,500 per carousel."
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "Always invoice 50% upfront upon contract signing and 50% within 14 days of publishing the live piece."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}